Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: rtl8821ce
Upstream-Contact: Smech <smechlabs@proton.me>
Source: https://github.com/Smech-Labs/rtl8821ce
Comment:
 Forked from https://github.com/tomaspinho/rtl8821ce, archived by its
 maintainer in 2026 with no successor, and patched to build against
 current kernels (cfg80211 wireless_dev-based ops, strncpy() removal,
 removed AppleTalk structs). Those patches are plain GPL-2 source and
 carried in the same files as the rest of the driver below.
 .
 This package is placed in non-free-firmware, not main, because of the
 two files called out below: they compile in opaque Realtek firmware
 microcode as C byte arrays (not loadable blobs fetched at runtime via
 request_firmware(), which is how most Realtek firmware is split out
 into the separate firmware-realtek package in main's reach). A GPL
 header on a byte array is not the same as having a preferred form for
 modification -- there is no human-authored source for that microcode
 in this repository, upstream's history, or anywhere else checked.
 Because it's linked directly into the built .ko rather than loaded
 separately, the built module as a whole has to follow the firmware,
 even though the surrounding driver source is genuinely free.

Files: *
Copyright: 2007-2020 Realtek Semiconductor Corp. All rights reserved.
License: GPL-2

Files: hal/phydm/rtl8821c/halhwimg8821c_fw.c
 hal/rtl8821c/hal8821c_fw.c
Copyright: 2007-2011 Realtek Corporation. All rights reserved.
License: GPL-2
Comment:
 These two files carry a GPL-2 header but their actual content is
 opaque firmware microcode for the 8821C's embedded MCU, expressed as
 raw C byte arrays (array_mp_8821c_fw_ap[], etc.) rather than anything
 a human wrote or could meaningfully modify. No corresponding source
 form is available. This is the reason the package as a whole sits in
 non-free-firmware instead of main -- see the top-level Comment field.

